# Cortical Hierarchy Category Coding — Meta-Audit

Survey of categorical neural representations across the full cortical hierarchy (V1 → PFC/OFC).

## Per-Region Summary

| Region | Status | Sources | Key Finding |
|--------|--------|---------|-------------|
| V1-V3 | PASS | 10 | Animacy/size decodable from V1 populations. Color categorization emerges. Categorical representations rare — high-dimensional code dominates |
| V4 | PASS | 10 | Mid-level hub: shape-texture continuum, color categories, category × attention interaction. 35% foveal units category-selective |
| LOC/ITC | PASS | 10 | Shape-dominant: weak single-neuron category tuning, strong at population level. Category trumps shape as organizing principle |
| MTL | PASS | 10 | Concept cells with semantic tuning curves. Region-based feature coding bridges vision to categories. Abstract semantic hierarchy |
| LIP/Parietal | PASS | 10 | Strongest category signals in the hierarchy. Causal role in perceptual decisions. Curved task-dependent manifolds |
| MFC/dACC | PASS | 10 | Separate decision axes for memory vs categorization. Task-set representations. Theta-phase locking to MTL for memory retrieval |
| PFC/OFC | PASS | 10 | OFC neurons categorically encode single decision variables (confidence, value). dlPFC for rule-based, vmPFC for prototype learning. Abstract category representations |

## Fundamentals

- Categorical coding at single-neuron level is **rare** outside primary sensory areas
- Population-level category information is **ubiquitous** even where single neurons show no category tuning
- **Hierarchy gradient**: dimensionality increases, clustering decreases from sensory → frontal
- **Two coding regimes**: low-dimensional categorical in sensory areas, high-dimensional mixed-selectivity in cognitive areas

## By Region

### V1-V3
- Animacy/real-world size decodable from V1 populations (PMC10312552)
- Color categorization boundaries present in V1/V2/V4 (Sah 1996)
- Spatial frequency → categorical representations in ~180ms (PMC6057270)
- Categorical clustering of color space emerges in V4v/VO1 (JNeurosci 33:15454)
- Overall: categorical structure rare, high-dimensional separability maximal (bioRxiv 2024)

### V4
- 35% foveal units show category selectivity (faces vs houses) — SciAdv
- Shape-texture coding continuum (JNeurosci 2019)
- Categorical working memory codes for color (bioRxiv 2021)
- Task context modulates feature selectivity (JNeurosci 42:6408)
- Functional domains for color, luminance, orientation (PMC4912377)

### LOC/ITC
- Human LOC: shape-dominant, ~3% single-channel category-only, 48% shape×category interaction (NatureComms 2024)
- Animate-inanimate primary organizing dimension, not aspect ratio (PMC10124953)
- Shape similarity > semantic membership for IT representations (PLOS CompBio 2013)
- Orthogonal shape/category gradients: shape in V1, category in anterior VTC (SciRep 2020)

### MTL (amygdala, hippocampus, EC, PHC)
- Concept cells: sparse, invariant semantic representations (NatureComms 2025)
- Region-based feature coding: neurons respond to feature-space regions, not categories per se (PMC11811184)
- Semantic tuning curves: graded, sigmoidal responses along semantic dimensions (bioRxiv 2025)
- Abstract hierarchy: fruit → food → natural things encoded at population level (PLOS Bio 2019)
- Concept cells flexibly encode abstract relations between concepts (PMC8545952)

### LIP / Parietal
- LIP shows strongest, earliest category signals — stronger than PFC (NatureNeuro 2012)
- Causal role: inactivation impairs categorical decisions (Science 2019, PMC10255012)
- Curved decision manifolds: task-dependent rotation in state space (PMC8273140)
- LIP vs MIP: LIP more involved in categorization itself, MIP in motor response (JNeurosci 2013)
- MST also shows robust category encoding (JNeurosci 2022)

### MFC (dACC, pre-SMA)
- Separate population subspaces for memory-based vs categorization-based decisions (Science 2020)
- Pre-SMA encodes categorical boundaries for time intervals (NatureComms 2018)
- dACC neurons encode cognitive load, conflict adaptation (PMC3416924)
- MFC-HA theta-phase locking selectively engaged during memory retrieval (Science 2020)
- Pre-SMA encodes integrated utility signal for value-based choice (NatureHumBehav 2023)

### PFC / OFC
- OFC neurons form ~9 categorical clusters, each encoding a single decision variable (Nature 2019)
- Decision variables: confidence, integrated value, reward size, previous outcome — categorically encoded (PLOS CompBio 2019)
- dlPFC: rule-based categorization; vmPFC: prototype learning, attention to diagnostic features (JNeurosci 44:34)
- Lateral PFC: abstract category representations for visual stimuli (Science 291:312)
- Value and choice are separable, stable population representations in OFC (NatureComms 2020)

## Meta-analyses

| Citation | Scope | Key Finding |
|----------|-------|-------------|
| Posani et al. 2024 (bioRxiv) | 43 cortical regions in mice | Categorical only in primary sensory; high-dimensional code elsewhere; max separability everywhere |
| Fusi, Miller & Rigotti 2016 (Curr Opin Neurobiol) | Review: mixed selectivity | High-dimensional representations enable flexible linear readout |
| Kourtzi & Connor 2011 (Annu Rev Neurosci) | Object representations | Shape, category, and adaptive coding across ventral stream |
| Freedman & Assad 2011 (Nat Neurosci) | Common mechanism review | Category and perceptual decisions share neural substrate in parietal |
| Moneta, Grossman & Schuck 2024 (TINS) | OFC/vmPFC | Task states and values integrated; mixed selectivity common |

## Gaps

- **Within-area microarchitecture**: how do categorical clusters form at columnar scale in humans? (only inferred from fMRI)
- **Cross-species homology**: human LOC ↔ macaque ITC/TE/TEO mapping still debated
- **Development**: how do categorical representations emerge during learning? (adult studies only)
- **Causal interactions**: most evidence correlational; inactivation/perturbation only in monkey LIP and PFC
- **Naturalistic stimuli**: most studies use controlled lab stimuli — how do categories work in natural vision?
- **Single-neuron human data**: only available from epilepsy patients (MTL, MFC, LOC) — surgical constraints
- **Within-category structure**: how are exemplars organized within a category representation?

